    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009-sch-1-sec-275b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "275B Emergency management person",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009#sch-1-sec-275b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009.pdf, p.7",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Part:\nemergency management person means a person who holds,\noccupies or performs the duties of an office or position specified\nunder subsection (2).\n\n(2) The Minister administering the Administrative Decisions (Judicial\nReview) Act 1977 may, by legislative instrument, specify either or\nboth of the following for the purposes of the definition of\nemergency management person in subsection (1) of this section:\n\n(a) offices;\n\n(b) positions.\n\n(3) Offices or positions established by or under a law of a State or\nTerritory may be specified under subsection (2).\n\n(4) Subsection (3) does not limit subsection (2).\n\n(5) Before making an instrument under subsection (2), the Minister\nadministering the Administrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act\n1977 must consult the Minister administering this Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In this Part:\nemergency management person means a person who holds,\noccupies or performs the duties of an office or position specified\nunder subsection (2).\n\n(2) The Minister administering the Administrative Decisions (Judicial\nReview) Act 1977 may, by legislative instrument, specify either or\nboth of the following for the purposes of the definition of\nemergency management person in subsection (1) of this section:\n\n(a) offices;\n\n(b) positions.\n\n(3) Offices or positions established by or under a law of a State or\nTerritory may be specified under subsection (2).\n\n(4) Subsection (3) does not limit subsection (2).\n\n(5) Before making an instrument under subsection (2), the Minister\nadministering the Administrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act\n1977 must consult the Minister administering this Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009-sch-1-sec-275b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009-sch-1-sec-275b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009-sch-1-sec-275b-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009-sch-1-sec-275b-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009-sch-1-sec-275b-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bb14a11a1fb3f2d28769cb91faee3646f319e69debaf071669ad53283f80abb6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009#sch-1-sec-275b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "275B Emergency management person",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 7,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Part:\nemergency management person means a person who holds,\noccupies or performs the duties of an office or position specified\nunder subsection (2).\n\n(2) The Minister administering the Administrative Decisions (Judicial\nReview) Act 1977 may, by legislative instrument, specify either or\nboth of the following for the purposes of the definition of\nemergency management person in subsection (1) of this section:\n\n(a) offices;\n\n(b) positions.\n\n(3) Offices or positions established by or under a law of a State or\nTerritory may be specified under subsection (2).\n\n(4) Subsection (3) does not limit subsection (2).\n\n(5) Before making an instrument under subsection (2), the Minister\nadministering the Administrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act\n1977 must consult the Minister administering this Act."
    },
