    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009-sch-1-sec-285a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "285A Data for emergency warnings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009#sch-1-sec-285a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 276 and 277 do not prohibit a disclosure by a person (the\ndiscloser) of information or a document if:\n\n(a) the information is, or the document consists of, information\n(including unlisted telephone numbers) contained in an\nintegrated public number database; and\n\n(b) the disclosure is made to an emergency management person;\nand\n\n(c) the emergency management person has given the discloser a\nwritten notice stating that the disclosure is for the purpose of\nthe information, or the contents of the document, being later\nused or disclosed for either or both of the following:\n\n(i) for a purpose connected with persons being alerted to an\nemergency or a likely emergency;\n\n(ii) for the purpose of reasonable testing of whether, in the\nevent of an emergency occurring, persons would be able\nto be alerted to that emergency.\n\n(1A) A notice given as mentioned in paragraph (1)(c) may cover one or\nmore disclosures (including each disclosure in a series of\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nData for emergency warnings  Part 1\n\n2009            5\ndisclosures under an arrangement between the discloser and the\nemergency management person).\n\n(1B) A notice given as mentioned in paragraph (1)(c) is not a legislative\ninstrument.\n\n(2) In this section:\nintegrated public number database means:\n\n(a) an integrated public number database maintained by Telstra\nas mentioned in Part 4 of Schedule 2; or\n\n(b) an integrated public number database maintained by a person\nas mentioned in section 472.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Sections 276 and 277 do not prohibit a disclosure by a person (the\ndiscloser) of information or a document if:\n\n(a) the information is, or the document consists of, information\n(including unlisted telephone numbers) contained in an\nintegrated public number database; and\n\n(b) the disclosure is made to an emergency management person;\nand\n\n(c) the emergency management person has given the discloser a\nwritten notice stating that the disclosure is for the purpose of\nthe information, or the contents of the document, being later\nused or disclosed for either or both of the following:\n\n(i) for a purpose connected with persons being alerted to an\nemergency or a likely emergency;\n\n(ii) for the purpose of reasonable testing of whether, in the\nevent of an emergency occurring, persons would be able\nto be alerted to that emergency.\n\n(1A) A notice given as mentioned in paragraph (1)(c) may cover one or\nmore disclosures (including each disclosure in a series of\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nData for emergency warnings  Part 1\n\n2009            5\ndisclosures under an arrangement between the discloser and the\nemergency management person).\n\n(1B) A notice given as mentioned in paragraph (1)(c) is not a legislative\ninstrument.\n\n(2) In this section:\nintegrated public number database means:\n\n(a) an integrated public number database maintained by Telstra\nas mentioned in Part 4 of Schedule 2; or\n\n(b) an integrated public number database maintained by a person\nas mentioned in section 472.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009-sch-1-sec-285a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009-sch-1-sec-285a-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009-sch-1-sec-285a-ss-1b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009-sch-1-sec-285a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a4e7d534bad8809e35b842a1c783e8aee0a10b22d680aecfdbd01c99203167c2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009#sch-1-sec-285a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "285A Data for emergency warnings",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 276 and 277 do not prohibit a disclosure by a person (the\ndiscloser) of information or a document if:\n\n(a) the information is, or the document consists of, information\n(including unlisted telephone numbers) contained in an\nintegrated public number database; and\n\n(b) the disclosure is made to an emergency management person;\nand\n\n(c) the emergency management person has given the discloser a\nwritten notice stating that the disclosure is for the purpose of\nthe information, or the contents of the document, being later\nused or disclosed for either or both of the following:\n\n(i) for a purpose connected with persons being alerted to an\nemergency or a likely emergency;\n\n(ii) for the purpose of reasonable testing of whether, in the\nevent of an emergency occurring, persons would be able\nto be alerted to that emergency.\n\n(1A) A notice given as mentioned in paragraph (1)(c) may cover one or\nmore disclosures (including each disclosure in a series of\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nData for emergency warnings  Part 1\n\n2009            5\ndisclosures under an arrangement between the discloser and the\nemergency management person).\n\n(1B) A notice given as mentioned in paragraph (1)(c) is not a legislative\ninstrument.\n\n(2) In this section:\nintegrated public number database means:\n\n(a) an integrated public number database maintained by Telstra\nas mentioned in Part 4 of Schedule 2; or\n\n(b) an integrated public number database maintained by a person\nas mentioned in section 472."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009-sch-1-sec-285a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "285A(1) Data for emergency warnings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
