    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009-sch-1-sec-295v",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "295V Use or disclosure of information by emergency management",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009#sch-1-sec-295v"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "persons\nLikely emergencies\n\n(1) If an emergency management person believes on reasonable\ngrounds that an emergency is likely to occur, the person may use or\ndisclose relevant information (other than the names of persons) for\na purpose connected with persons being alerted to that likely\nemergency.\nActual emergencies\n\n(2) If an emergency occurs, an emergency management person may\nuse or disclose relevant information (other than the names of\npersons) for a purpose connected with persons being alerted to that\nemergency.\nTesting\n\n(3) An emergency management person may use or disclose relevant\ninformation (other than the names of persons) for the purpose of\nreasonable testing of whether, in the event of an emergency\noccurring, persons would be able to be alerted to that emergency.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "persons\nLikely emergencies\n\n(1) If an emergency management person believes on reasonable\ngrounds that an emergency is likely to occur, the person may use or\ndisclose relevant information (other than the names of persons) for\na purpose connected with persons being alerted to that likely\nemergency.\nActual emergencies\n\n(2) If an emergency occurs, an emergency management person may\nuse or disclose relevant information (other than the names of\npersons) for a purpose connected with persons being alerted to that\nemergency.\nTesting\n\n(3) An emergency management person may use or disclose relevant\ninformation (other than the names of persons) for the purpose of\nreasonable testing of whether, in the event of an emergency\noccurring, persons would be able to be alerted to that emergency.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009-sch-1-sec-295v-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009-sch-1-sec-295v-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009-sch-1-sec-295v-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4f8e8d708ef0ee1b7cc9efbd039efe39a9d94d385793f874e9ff266f8b19b895"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009#sch-1-sec-295v",
