      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "(3) An emergency management person may use or disclose relevant\ninformation (other than the names of persons) for the purpose of\nreasonable testing of whether, in the event of an emergency\noccurring, persons would be able to be alerted to that emergency.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(3) An emergency management person may use or disclose relevant\ninformation (other than the names of persons) for the purpose of\nreasonable testing of whether, in the event of an emergency\noccurring, persons would be able to be alerted to that emergency.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "values:partOf": {
