    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009-sch-1-sec-295zb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "295ZB Reports of access",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009#sch-1-sec-295zb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an emergency management person discloses relevant\ninformation, the person must give a written report to the Minister\nadministering the Administrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act\n1977 and to the ACMA that covers the following matters:\n\n(a) if the disclosure occurred under subsection 295V(1) or (2)—a\ndescription of the emergency or likely emergency concerned\nand its location;\n\n(b) in any case—the number of telephone numbers that were\ndisclosed and the day that disclosure occurred;\n\n(c) in any case—the number of persons to whom the emergency\nmanagement person disclosed those numbers and the purpose\nof each disclosure.\n\n(2) The emergency management person must give the report to the\nMinister administering the Administrative Decisions (Judicial\nReview) Act 1977 and to the ACMA as soon as practicable after the\nlast disclosure referred to in paragraph (1)(c) of this section occurs\n(disregarding section 295Y).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If an emergency management person discloses relevant\ninformation, the person must give a written report to the Minister\nadministering the Administrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act\n1977 and to the ACMA that covers the following matters:\n\n(a) if the disclosure occurred under subsection 295V(1) or (2)—a\ndescription of the emergency or likely emergency concerned\nand its location;\n\n(b) in any case—the number of telephone numbers that were\ndisclosed and the day that disclosure occurred;\n\n(c) in any case—the number of persons to whom the emergency\nmanagement person disclosed those numbers and the purpose\nof each disclosure.\n\n(2) The emergency management person must give the report to the\nMinister administering the Administrative Decisions (Judicial\nReview) Act 1977 and to the ACMA as soon as practicable after the\nlast disclosure referred to in paragraph (1)(c) of this section occurs\n(disregarding section 295Y).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009-sch-1-sec-295zb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009-sch-1-sec-295zb-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f37d80685039808ee3c20b05edb419a57e82a5fe52f046bf083f5f9eadf64342"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2009#sch-1-sec-295zb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "295ZB Reports of access",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an emergency management person discloses relevant\ninformation, the person must give a written report to the Minister\nadministering the Administrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act\n1977 and to the ACMA that covers the following matters:\n\n(a) if the disclosure occurred under subsection 295V(1) or (2)—a\ndescription of the emergency or likely emergency concerned\nand its location;\n\n(b) in any case—the number of telephone numbers that were\ndisclosed and the day that disclosure occurred;\n\n(c) in any case—the number of persons to whom the emergency\nmanagement person disclosed those numbers and the purpose\nof each disclosure.\n\n(2) The emergency management person must give the report to the\nMinister administering the Administrative Decisions (Judicial\nReview) Act 1977 and to the ACMA as soon as practicable after the\nlast disclosure referred to in paragraph (1)(c) of this section occurs\n(disregarding section 295Y)."
    },
